      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-wammft",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "1. Scoring a Dish"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-vmavny",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>Each ingredient is scored on what the player got right, then scaled by how much it matters to the recipe.</p><p><code style=\"color: rgb(250, 110, 110); font-weight: bold;\">Type Value = (Ingredient + Shape + State) × Weight × Quantity</code></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-y5pdrr",
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "",
          "columns": [
            "Axis",
            "What it Checks",
            "Primary (Main)",
            "Secondary (Topping)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Ingredient",
              "The right ingredient",
              "2,000",
              "750"
            ],
            [
              "Shape",
              "The right cut or format",
              "0",
              "250"
            ],
            [
              "State",
              "The right state, e.g. cooked",
              "0 - 40",
              "0 - 40"
            ],
            [
              "Weight",
              "How much this ingredient matters",
              "x1 - 10",
              "x1 - 10"
            ],
            [
              "Quantity",
              "How many the recipe needs",
              "1 - 5",
              "1 - 5"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-oqrxj0",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>The <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Phase Base</span> is the primary and secondary values added together. Players then earn an <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Order Bonus</span> for a 100% correct dish and a <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Time Bonus</span> for the time left on the clock.</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(250, 110, 110); font-weight: bold;\"><code>Final Score = Phase Base + Order Bonus + Time Bonus</code></span></p><p>Because the main ingredient is worth half the dish, an order with the wrong primary can never reach a passing grade.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-3vm3av",
          "type": "sheet",
          "source": "file",
          "sheetId": "1emay3wnJ4YmshKu7J8i51iLl7vpS0AlV_xu8J50NPkg",
          "height": "medium",
          "gid": "1444584704"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-9bx2p7",
          "type": "spacer",
          "size": "sm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-maisrd",
      "type": "section",
      "background": "none",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-zid1dg",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "2. Star Tiers"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-kt712z",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>Stars are set as a share of each phase's maximum score, so the same rules work for every recipe whatever its size.</p>"
        },
        {
