      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-9tyj2g",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "3. Simulating World 1"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-w8zjsy",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>I ran all five World 1 phases through the model with realistic delivery times, to check how the tiers behave before any playtest.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-iqz9bc",
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "",
          "columns": [
            "Phase",
            "Phase Base",
            "Phase Time",
            "Delivered At",
            "Score vs. Max",
            "Tier"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1 - 1",
              "4,000",
              "120 s",
              "80 s",
              "99.95%",
              "★★★"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 2",
              "1,950",
              "90 s",
              "55 s",
              "99.94%",
              "★★★"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 3",
              "4,480",
              "270 s",
              "210 s",
              "99.89%",
              "★★★"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 4",
              "5,140",
              "150 s",
              "110 s",
              "99.95%",
              "★★★"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 5",
              "2,700",
              "340 s",
              "250 s",
              "99.79%",
              "★★★"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-i0flqi",
          "type": "spacer",
          "size": "sm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-tg8p40",
      "type": "section",
      "background": "none",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-1sey8w",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Iteration Case"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-ue1scz",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Problem:</span> In the World 1 simulation, every perfect order landed at about 99.9% of the maximum, so ★★★ and nothing more. No delivery time could reach the Golden Fork.</p><p><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Cause:</span> Two parts of the formula worked against each other.</p><p></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">The Time Bonus was too Small to Matter:</span> At 0.025 points per second left, the most time could ever add was 2–9 points on a 2,000–5,000 point dish. A fast, perfect order and a last-second one scored almost the same.</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">The Golden Fork Assumed a Full Clock:</span> The maximum score counted every second of the phase as unused, so it required delivering at 0 seconds, which is impossible.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Options Considered:</span></div><div><ul><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Raise the Bonus Rate.</span> Rejected: even the top of its range (0.5) adds only about 4%, and the bonus would still scale with phase length instead of recipe size.</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Lower the Golden Fork to 99%.</span> Rejected: it would hide the problem; speed still wouldn't matter.</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Make the Time Bonus a share of the dish, and set the Golden Fork at a par time.</span> Chosen.</li></ul><div><br></div></div><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Fix:</span> The Time Bonus becomes a pool worth 25% of the Phase Base, paid out in proportion to the time left. The Golden Fork is the score of a perfect order delivered at par time, set at half the phase clock.</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color: rgb(250, 110, 110); font-weight: bold;\"><code>Time Bonus = 25% × Phase Base × (Time Left ÷ Phase Time) Golden Fork = Phase Base + Order Bonus + Time Bonus at par</code></span></div><div><span style=\"color: rgb(250, 110, 110); font-weight: bold;\"><code><br></code></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\"><span class=\"big\">Result (Simulated):</span></span></div><p></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-zavabc",
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "",
          "columns": [
            "Phase",
            "Golden Fork",
            "Perfect, Realistic Time",
            "Perfect, Last Second",
            "Small Mistake (Loses Order Bonus), Realistic Time"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1 - 1",
              "4,800",
              "96.5%",
              "89.6%",
              "90.3%"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 2",
              "2,494",
              "97.8%",
              "90.2%",
              "85.8%"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 3",
              "5,340",
              "94.2%",
              "89.5%",
              "88.6%"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 4",
              "6,082",
              "95.1%",
              "89.4%",
              "90.1%"
            ],
            [
              "1 - 5",
              "3,338",
              "95.2%",
              "89.9%",
              "86.3%"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-dd9oj4",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>Speed now matters: perfect orders range from about 89% to 98% depending on how fast they arrive, and the Golden Fork is earned by beating par time. Accuracy still comes first: a slow perfect order still clears ★★★, and an order missing its main ingredient still can't pass.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-3f34be",
          "type": "spacer",
          "size": "sm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-vd8vzu",
      "type": "section",
      "background": "none",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-310vpd",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "4. Playtesting and UX"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-x2mlst",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p>I ran closed and open playtests, including at live events, owned the UX process, and ran usability tests. After each delivery, I analysed the playtests and presented adjustments to the team. I also worked with art and UI on readability, and with engineering on the 3C.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-x0oc84",
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "",
          "columns": [
            "",
            ""
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Formats",
              "Closed tests, open tests, live events"
            ],
            [
              "Testers",
              "Up to 50 testers throughout events, ranging from 17 to 55 years"
            ],
            [
              "What I watched",
              "Whether teams talked or went silent, where they got stuck, how they read the score"
            ],
            [
              "What came out",
              "Adjustments presented to the team after each delivery"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-2qtxwo",
          "type": "spacer",
          "size": "sm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-yzgwzz",
      "type": "section",
      "background": "none",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-h2hm96",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Decisions and Trade-Offs"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-hk5ab6",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p><ul><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Stars as a % of max over fixed scores</span>. Every recipe uses the same thresholds, at the cost of players not comparing raw scores across phases.</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Primary worth half the dish</span>. It makes the main ingredient a hard gate, though a perfect side dish can't rescue a wrong main.</li><li><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">A par time for the Golden Fork</span>. It gives top players a clear target, but par times need tuning per phase in playtests.</li></ul></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-rd18vc",
          "type": "spacer",
          "size": "sm"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-6edsqp",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Results"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-1mca4x",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p><ul><li>One scoring formula and one set of star rules covering every recipe in World 1.</li><li>A simulation that caught an unreachable top reward and a Time Bonus too small to matter, before playtests.</li></ul></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-vqf5se",
          "type": "spacer",
          "size": "sm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-e3rgam",
      "type": "section",
      "background": "none",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "b-61evpx",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Looking Back"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-75vv9j",
          "type": "text",
          "html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">What Worked: </span>Defining stars as a share of each phase's maximum, which made five very different recipes comparable.</p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">What I'd Do Differently: </span>Simulate the extremes (fastest, slowest and wrong orders) from the start, not only realistic deliveries. The time-bonus issue only shows when you compare them.</p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">What I Learned: </span>A bonus that's too small doesn't make a game easier; it makes a whole skill invisible.</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5g4a3f",
          "type": "sheet",
          "source": "file",
